{
  "Version": 2,
  "Name": "Young1961-T2-n150-maxflat-k3",
  "Source": "L. Young, \"Synthesis of multiple antireflection films over a prescribed frequency band,\" J. Opt. Soc. Am. 51, 967-974 (1961). doi:10.1364/JOSA.51.000967 - Table II p. 973 (Maximally flat filters, n = 1.50, k = 3: n1 = 1.05202) and Eq. (30)",
  "Notes": "Table II maximally flat (binomial) 3-layer AR coating from air to n = 1.50.\nSpecification: Maximally flat response (Fig. 2b): reflection zero of multiplicity 2k at band centre.\nReported: Eq. (11): insertion loss P_L = 1 + [(n-1)^2/4n] cos^6(theta), theta = (pi/2)(550/lambda), so R = x/(1+x) with x = (1/24) cos^6(theta): R = 0 at 550 nm, R = 0.04 at 275 nm (half wave), e.g. R = 5.2e-3 at 366.67 and 1100 nm (theta = 135 and 45 deg, x = 0.125/24; derived, not printed). Table II binomial values: n1 = 1.05202 for n = 1.50.\nNotes: As Young1961-T2-n150-W060-k2. band_nm [366.67, 1100] is only a plotting range; the maximally flat design has no bandwidth parameter. n2, n3 from Eq. (30).\nLayers from Table II p. 973 (Maximally flat filters, n = 1.50, k = 3: n1 = 1.05202) and Eq. (30); layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours R 2.6e-11 at 550 nm, 5.18e-3 at 366.7 nm; paper R 0 at 550 nm and 5.2e-3 at 366.7 nm (Eq. 11).",
